  "prefLabel": "Ins 2701.13 Enforcement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 2701.13 Enforcement. If the commissioner determines that a health carrier has not contracted with a sufficient number of participating providers to assure that covered persons have accessible health care services in a geographic area or that a health carrier’s health care certification of compliance report does not assure reasonable access to covered benefits, the commissioner shall issue an order requiring the health carrier to institute a corrective action, or shall use other enforcement powers under RSA 420-J to ensure that covered persons have access to covered benefits.\n\nSource. #12565, eff 8-1-18 (formerly Ins 2701.10)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins2700.html"
